Drop GLB files here. Names and node contracts: ../README.md

  eeri_v1.glb        hipL hipR body armL armR head
  excavator_v1.glb   house boom stick bucket seat step wheels beacon
  bank_v1.glb        state0 state1 state2
  girder_v1.glb      state0 state1 state2 grip
  wall_v1.glb        state0 state1 state2

Then flip that entry's "status" to "live" in ../manifest.json and bump
the manifest "v". Nothing else changes.

Note for generated models (Meshy and friends): a text-to-3D result is
normally ONE smooth-shaded mesh with PBR textures and no useful node
names. It will load, fail the contract, and the game will keep its
placeholder. Split it into the named parts, put each pivot on the real
hinge, flatten the normals and drop the PBR maps before exporting.
